===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|linguistics}} In such writing systems as the [[Chinese]] writing system, the portion of a [[phono-semantic]] character that provides an indication of its meaning; ''contrasted with'' [[phonetic]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|title=San tzu ching explicated, the classical initiation to classic Chinese couplet I to XI|author=Friedrich Alexander Bischoff, Yinglin Wang|page=21 |ISBN= |passage=Its '''semantic''' is polysyllabic, viz. it uses the word formations of spoken Chinese.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=Love and War in Ancient China: Voices from the Shijing|author=William S-Y. Wang|page=25 |ISBN= |passage=In this particular case, the '''semantic''' is on the left of its host sinogram.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|title=Understanding Chinese Characters|author=Vladimir Skultety|page= |ISBN= |passage=The 亻(人) ren2 'person' '''semantic''' has been replaced by 氵(水) shui3 'water' '''semantic''' in浸, but帚 zhou3 'broom' has phonetically or semantically nothing to do with 浸 and is just a residue of 侵 after亻(人) ren2 'person' has been removed.}}

